// THE ONE PLACE A SCRIPT SAYS "that doesn't do anything", and so the one place a use-on can be
// handed to the other item.
//
// "Use a on b" reaches only ONE of the two items' triggers - b's, b being whichever one the player
// clicked second - so a script that does not recognise its partner used to end the click there.
// That is why a chisel used on a serpentine visage carved a helm and a visage used on a chisel did
// nothing: [opheldu,chisel] has a case list and the visage was not on it. 963 pairs of items worked
// one way round only (Engine-TS/tools/sim/opheldu.ts).
//
// ^dm_default IS that refusal - all 787 of its call sites mean "these two do not go together" -
// so it is exactly the right place to ask. opheldu_decline hands the click to the other half and
// returns true, and this says nothing; it returns false when there is nobody left to ask, when the
// click has already been handed over once, or when the caller is not a use-on at all, and then the
// message is printed as it always was.
[proc,displaymessage](int $index)
if ($index = ^dm_default & opheldu_decline = true) {
    return;
}
mes(enum(int, string, displaymessage_enum, $index));
